A||||7||wwh0001||Idle Problems||||1||
Z||000000||wwh0001||06-13-2000||01:54 PM||||I have an 87Gt that has had idle problems for awhile.The issue is a fast idle that won't come down, that is, most of the time. I have replced the IAC and the TPS, MAP, temp sensor, cold start switch. EGR valve , tube and solonoid are good, no vaccuum leaks.<BR>Problem occurs , at times, when engine is either warm or cold. Problem is that the idle will go up to 1600 to 2500 RPMS when driving, 0r sometmes when started the idle will go up that high and not come down. In a process of elimination I replaced the parts above. Each time disconnecting the battery to clear the ECM. And each time a part was replaced the idle would go back to normal levels; that is until you drive it. Then for no reason the idle will go up and stick. I have now discovered that when this happens and I disconnect the battery the idle will go back to normal levels and stay there until it is driven. Syptoms would remind me of a sticking choke if it had one since sometimes ( not always) the idle will go back to normal levels if I just pump the pedal a couple of times. (And no the cables are not sticking. Anyone have any ideas ? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||06-13-2000||03:30 PM||||Could the battery be on its way out?  See if dash voltmeter shows lower voltage with battery cable connected.  Maybe it's idling fast trying to charge a battery that has internal problems.<P>Swap battery with a known good one, if handy, and see what happens.<P>Or maybe loose alternator belt?<P>Pure guessing ...     <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-13-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000002||dman||06-13-2000||03:35 PM||||Hi wwh0001. Hmm...have you checked your throttle body? Sometimes they get really dirty. In fact they can get -very- dirty and gummed up. I make this guess based on your statement, "the idle will go back to normal levels if I just pump the pedal a couple of times"<P>Personally I find it easier to just remove it and clean it, but others here have stated that you can get good results using spray on carb cleaner --- they have also said that you need to be careful you don't accidentally shoot the straw off the can and into your intake plenum. Good advice.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||wwh0001||06-13-2000||04:08 PM||||Thanks for the suggestions. The battery is new and is holding a full charge. I have cleaned the throttle body as well. The strange thing is that the idle will go back to normal somtimes when I pump it, but not always. However, every time the idle is too high, I shut the engine off, then disconnect the battery and then reconnect the battery and start again. the idle will always go back to normal until it has be driven awhile. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||06-14-2000||12:49 PM||||...<p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-14-2000).]||||reg||5
