Z||000006||StuGood||06-14-2000||01:03 PM||||Suggestion:<BR>Next time it idles fast, unplug IAC.  Stop engine and remove IAC.<P>If IAC plunger is fully retracted, you know that it's idling fast because ECM says so.||||reg||3
Z||000007||Motorhead||06-15-2000||08:40 PM||||Just a thought thrown in for the hell of it.<BR>The gospel according to Ogre says, "the brain has a learning curve".<BR>After installing a new MAP and clearing the ECM idle was eratic.<BR>A few miles of driving, and the thing figured out what it was supposed to be doing and settled into a nice consistant 900 RPM.  Patiance paid off!<BR>dman is right! Cleanliness is next to Godliness!!<BR>My 2 cents!  For what it's worth.||||reg||1
